  "note": "Election of the whole Londonderry Corporation (six councillors and two aldermen for each of the five wards), poll Friday 15 January 1926. The Labour Party, with Nationalist support, contested all five wards; the Journal gives the new Corporation as 16 Labour and 24 Unionist (Derry Journal, 18 January 1926). The Unionist aldermen for East, North and Waterside were returned unopposed and the South aldermanships were contested. M'Glinchey's 1,381 is the Londonderry Sentinel's figure (19 January, read on the page image), which fits the ward's councillor poll; the Journal's figure read earlier as 1,831 is taken as a misprint or misreading. Smyth's 788 is the Journal's figure (the Sentinel's middle digit is damaged). Spoiled papers 126 (Sentinel)."
